 variety and a  lot of powers for players but not get in  that situation so the idea of hey I'm  using one set of powers when I switch to  another was kind of it was a design  point for us to allow you to have a lot  of variety but do it in a way that  didn't kind of big you're not overwhelm  you all at once yeah I goofed out like  really really big-time the minute that I  saw that we were actually going to be  able to have multiple power set about  power sets because it's just awesome for  us as animators it's like the kid in the  candy store because because really okay  we can think about moving through the  environment a different way per power  you know powers are such an intrinsic  part of what's fun about the game  whether they're offensive or traversal  or you know creative they it's so  important that we give you lots of those  powers and so the idea of having a  character who could draw other power  sits into themselves was a big design  point as well  but what about his backstory and no I'm  not talking about how he got his  superpowers I'm talking about how Delson  the character came to be in the first  place  game director Nate Fox took the reins on  this one in fact we chose on infamous  second son to make a new character for  the game because we looked at trophy  data from infamous to where players  decided to sacrifice whole for the  greater good he thought will honor that  choice we're very interested in how  people make choices and we want to make  them potent it seems like such a rare  occurrence for an established series  like to us to go and swap protagonists I  wrote the endings of the infamous 2 and  I wanted it to be the evil one where he  stayed alive but kind of honoring what  people wanted he said ok we will not do  that we'll do the good ending and that  led us through Delson which was great  because we get an all-new origin story  we get a hero with new powers and as  somebody that may be new to the  franchise it's perfect you don't have 